At Feedzai, we're building a world of safer money. A world where financial institutions move faster than criminals. Where the payments that fund real lives through salaries, savings, and businesses are protected in real time. We use trusted AI to detect and prevent financial crime, fraud, and money laundering at scale: the world's top banks, payment networks, and acquirers trust our technology to safeguard more than one billion consumers and $9 trillion in payment volume every year.

Feedzai is a Series D company and has raised $282M to date. With a valuation of $2 billion, our technology protects 1 billion consumers and 90 billion transactions each year.

The Customer Success Engineering team is responsible for ensuring that Feedzai solutions are successfully implemented, integrated, optimized, and supported throughout the customer lifecycle. Our mission is to build new product capabilities, but to deeply understand the product and leverage its full potential to solve complex customer problems. We work directly with enterprise customers, translating business requirements into scalable technical solutions while ensuring successful deployments, operational excellence, and long-term customer success.


YOU

As an Advanced Customer Success Engineer, you are an experienced software engineer with a strong implementation mindset. You are comfortable reading, writing, and debugging production-quality code, but your primary focus is delivering successful customer solutions through implementation, integrations, troubleshooting, performance optimization, and technical leadership.

You will serve as a trusted technical advisor for our customers and a technical reference within Customer Success, collaborating closely with Product Engineering, Product Management, Customer Success Managers, and customer technical teams.


YOUR DAY-TO-DAY

 * Design and implement technical solutions that maximize the value of the Feedzai platform;
 * Configure, customize, and extend customer solutions using Java, SQL, and platform configuration;
 * Build and maintain integrations using REST APIs, messaging systems, event-driven architectures, and file processing;
 * Troubleshoot complex production issues across application, database, infrastructure, and integration layers;
 * Analyze and optimize application performance, scalability, and operational reliability;
 * Lead technical activities during implementations, upgrades, migrations, and production go-lives;
 * Support enterprise customers throughout the implementation and post-production lifecycle;
 * Review solution designs and implementation approaches to ensure alignment with Feedzai best practices;
 * Mentor other engineers and contribute to reusable implementation assets, documentation, and engineering standards;
 * Collaborate with Product Engineering by providing feedback based on real customer implementations and operational experience;


YOU HAVE & YOU KNOW-HOW

 * 7+ years of professional software engineering experience;
 * Strong Java development skills with the ability to understand, customize, and debug complex applications;
 * Strong SQL knowledge and database troubleshooting experience;
 * Experience designing and implementing enterprise software integrations;
 * Experience working with REST APIs, messaging platforms, asynchronous systems, and file-based integrations;
 * Experience with cloud platforms (AWS preferred);
 * Strong troubleshooting and root cause analysis skills in production environments;
 * Experience analyzing Java application performance (thread dumps, heap analysis, JVM tuning);
 * Solid understanding of distributed systems, software architecture, scalability, and performance;
 * Excellent communication skills and the ability to work directly with customer engineering teams;
 * Ability to balance hands-on technical work with customer-facing responsibilities;
 * Experience in fraud prevention, financial services, or risk management platforms (nice to have);
 * Experience with Kubernetes and containerized applications (nice to have);
 * Experience with PostgreSQL and NoSQL databases (nice to have);

The Customer Success Team is responsible for delivering our product to our clients. This includes configuration, solution development, and risk strategy to enable them to address their pain points. We collaborate with our clients to ensure they have the right solution, build out a strategy and training plan for them, and then support them through each phase of our client lifecycle. We grow at a fast clip and believe no challenge is too big or too small. Therefore, we have an open environment that encourages us to lean in, try new things, and discover our potential. Join us!

#LI-Remote #LI-BX1

----------------------------------------

Your First 30-Days at Feedzai:

You will be immersed in our brand with training, connections, and one-on-one time with your manager. You may shadow your colleagues virtually or onsite at an office depending on where you work as you are supported through your Feedzai journey. In addition, you will have access to a ton of information to give you history, context, and all the knowledge you can handle about Feedzai and the team. Finally, you will start working on projects and collaborating on work currently being done. We can't wait to have you join the team!

Life at Feedzai Instagram

Feedzai Culture

----------------------------------------

Feedzai is an Equal Opportunity Employer and we value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.

Feedzai does not accept unsolicited resumes from recruiters or employment agencies.

Feedzai will use the personal data you provide us with by filling out this form for reviewing your application and to potentially negotiate a contract with you. Your personal data will be retained by Feedzai for 24 months following your application. Please see our Privacy Notice available at https://www.feedzai.com/legal/feedzai-candidate-privacy-policy/ and https://www.feedzai.com/legal/feedzai-california-candidates-privacy-policy/ for more information on how we process your personal data.

WHAT IS TEACHABLE?

Teachable is the platform for experts and businesses who take education seriously. In a world where anyone can ask AI for information, we're the home for those who educate with purpose, modernity, and humanity. We help experts and businesses scale their impact and operations through courses, coaching, and digital downloads that students actually love. From a finance expert teaching Python for investment analysis to a multilingual coach offering business Spanish for executives, Teachable powers human-led learning that drives student trust, connection, and results. With a sleek, intuitive interface and AI as a time-saving partner, the platform enables transformative education rooted in real-world experience. Teachable experts have lived it—that's why they teach it.Are you ready to join a dynamic, cross-cultural team at an exciting turning point in our company’s journey?

Part of the global Hotmart Company portfolio, whose platforms have helped creators, experts, and businesses earn more than $10 billion, Teachable continues to cement itself as a true industry leader. Together, Teachable and Hotmart are delivering market-leading products that prioritize student outcomes, business growth, and flexibility. If you have big ideas, relish the chance to challenge convention, and deeply believe in the power of real-world learning to shape the future, we want you on our team!

Teachable is a platform for creators who want to build a more impactful business through courses, coaching, downloadable content, and community. With Teachable, creators can engage their online audiences and get paid-on their own terms. Today, tens of thousands of creators use Teachable to share their knowledge and, to date, have reached more than 46 million students around the world.

Are you ready to join a dynamic, cross-cultural team at an exciting turning point in our company’s journey? Now part of the global Hotmart Company portfolio, Teachable continues to take the creator economy by storm as a true industry leader. Together, Teachable and Hotmart are delivering market-leading products that prioritize creator control and flexibility, alongside meaningful partnership and support from our team. If you have big ideas, relish the chance to challenge convention, and deeply believe in the power of creators to shape the future, we want you on our team!

----------------------------------------

What is the role?

We’re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead and grow the engineers within our team. This inkividual will balance people management, delivery leadership, and cross-functional collaboration to ensure our team delivers high-impact projects that support Teachable’s business goals.

This contract is CLT and paid in $BRL.

----------------------------------------

What You'll Bring:

 * Manage, coach, and mentor more than 6 software engineers at the same time, providing performance feedback, and helping them develop their careers;
 * Knowledge in developing and managing web applications;
 * Establish and improve department processes in all areas including software development, operational efficiency, and delivery to achieve operational excellence;
 * Partner with Engineering leadership to help determine Engineering department strategy, tackle team-wide inefficiencies, and promote a culture of continuous improvement;
 * Drive management initiatives across the Engineering department and Technology organization, e.g hiring, career development, policies, budgets, etc;
 * Engage in sponsorship of Engineering-wide guilds, projects, and activities;
 * Collaborate and communicate with other pods and functions (Product Management, Product Design, Marketing) on cross-team and cross-functional initiatives;
 * Lead successful development and delivery of pod projects and operations;
 * Partner with engineering leadership to help determine Engineering-wide department strategy, tackle department-wide inefficiencies;
 * Work on remote, distributed teams;
 * Upholds Teachable values, including building and growing as part of a diverse team.

----------------------------------------


KEY REQUIREMENTS:

 * 5+ years of software engineering experience, with 1-2+ years of combined tech leadership or people management;
 * Proficient at project management; has a track record of making tradeoffs to deliver projects on time, with a high degree quality, and with a focus on achieving business goals;
 * Experience leading technical initiatives with impact across multiple teams or domains;
 * Thrives in ambiguity and can make forward progress in situations when given minimal guidance;
 * The relentless drive for continuous improvement and ownership with proven ability to instill in their teams;
 * Experience mentoring individual contributors of different seniority levels and specializations;
 * Has effectively recruited, hired, and led diverse engineering teams;
 * Knowledge in Ruby on Rails, Go and React (nice to have).

----------------------------------------


ADDITIONAL DETAILS:

At Teachable, we are committed to providing fair and competitive pay (using market data to inform our pay bands), rewarding high performance, and ensuring all employees have the opportunity and ability to impact Teachable’s overall company value. Base salaries will be reviewed at regular intervals throughout the year, typically following performance review cycles currently conducted annually or in conjunction with a promotion.

While Teachable maintains our NY office for local employees to use, we operate as a remote-first culture in order to give our employees added flexibility. In order to maintain connection and create a community beyond the screen, Teachable holds in-person events throughout the year, where employees and teams can come together for bonding, strategic alignment, goal-setting, and celebrations!

----------------------------------------

Teachable encourages individuals from a broad diversity of backgrounds to apply for positions. We are an equal opportunity employer, meaning we're committed to a fair and consistent interview process. Please tell us in your application if you require an accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job.

Please note that we will never request payment or bank account information at any stage of the recruitment process. As we continue to grow our teams, we urge you to be cautious of fraudulent job postings or recruitment activities that misuse our company name and information. Please protect your personal information during any recruitment process. While Monks may contact potential candidates via LinkedIn, all applications must be submitted through our official website (monks.com/careers).

Hello,

We’re delighted by your interest in joining Monks’ Hub team! :)

We are Monks’ International Media Hub, the area responsible for handling international digital marketing projects in collaboration with other agencies in the S4 group.

We are seeking Performance Media Specialists to join our team and set the standard for high-performance global campaign strategies. As a Specialist, you will be the focal point for performance media strategies on international projects.

If you have a strong data-driven mindset, experience as a Paid Media Specialist, and advanced English proficiency, this opportunity could be yours!




In your day-to-day work, your main activities will be:

 * Actively participate in meetings with clients and key stakeholders, ensuring that expectations and needs are understood and met; proactively demonstrate accountability and interest in client management;
 * Develop and implement effective digital marketing strategies across multiple channels, such as Google Ads, Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, TikTok, and programmatic, optimizing results and aligning with business objectives;
 * Create media plans that maximize campaign impact and achieve established KPIs;
 * Produce campaign performance reports using tools like Excel, Google Sheets, and Looker Studio;
 * Assist the team in monitoring and executing campaigns, from launch to final report delivery, ensuring deliverables align with projections and targets;
 * Develop and optimize performance ads in the CPC/PPC model;
 * Organize demands and reallocate to other project members when necessary, responsible for project management and routines;
 * Assist in the technical evolution of peers and other team members involved in the project.

For the Performance Media Specialist position, the requirements and expectations are:

 * Advanced or Fluent English: Essential for effective communication in an international environment and with global stakeholders;
 * Expertise in Digital Performance Media: Solid experience in creating, optimizing, and managing campaigns across multiple digital media platforms, including Google Ads, Meta Ads (Facebook and Instagram), TikTok, Pinterest, and Programmatic;
 * Data-driven: Analyze paid campaign results to inform strategic decisions and optimizations aimed at improving performance;
 * Autonomy and Proactivity: Ability to make independent decisions, take initiative, and manage complex scenarios effectively;
 * Commitment to Deadlines and Results: Ability to manage multiple demands and deliver results within established deadlines, with a high level of accountability.

Joining the Media Hub, you will have the opportunity to:

 * Build an International Career: Expand your footprint in the Performance Media field in a global and dynamic environment;
 * Connect with International Clients: Collaborate directly with clients from different markets around the world, enriching your experience;
 * Learn Cutting-Edge Tools: Develop in technologies and media platforms used in international markets, broadening your toolkit and performance techniques.




Tools and methodologies used:

 * Google Ads, Meta Ads, TikTok Ads, Google Suite, and other Paid Media platforms as needed;
 * In some cases, SA360, DV360, CM360, Google Analytics, Looker Studio, Excel;
 * For communication and organization: Slack, Gmail, Asana, among others as necessary;
 * AI tools, both internal and other organization-approved tools;
 * Data analysis, daily meetings (Dailies), 1-on-1s, active and continuous learning.

What can be learned and developed:

 * English language development and greater knowledge of the American market and other regions;
 * Opportunity to develop storytelling presentation skills and conflict management;
 * Technical and strategic knowledge across different paid media platforms;
 * Demand organization, task delegation, and expectation alignment;
 * Experience in a multinational company with diverse cultures;
 * Knowledge of AI and how to apply it to improve results and efficiency gains;
 * Access to platform certifications on an ongoing basis




What We Offer

Here at Monks, we support and value our people not only with excellent benefits but also by prioritizing wellbeing and development!

Flexible meal and grocery allowance card;

Health insurance;

Dental insurance;

Flexible working hours and location;

Home office allowance paid through payroll (regardless of whether the work model is hybrid or 100% remote);

Monthly childcare assistance for people with children up to 5 years and 11 months old;

️ Access to various gyms through partner platform;

Birthday day off with no salary deduction;

Parental leave: 180 days for the pregnant people and 30 days for the non-pregnant people;

♿ Atypical parental care alowance for caregiver-parents of children with disabilities or neurodiversity;

Physical and emotional health and wellbeing platforms;

Free consultancy for Social and Psychological Assistance, Legal Guidance, and Financial Advice;

Reduced electricity costs through renewable energy sources;

Free SESC membership providing access to culture, education, health, sports, leisure, and assistance;

Partnerships with educational institutions;

Our Talent Development team is ready to help you in your pursuit of knowledge and growth so you can continue advancing here;

Community groups to connect, share experiences, and be part of this amazing culture.

These benefits may be subject to change at the time of hiring.

Monks LGPD

At Monks, we include the LGPD (Brazilian General Data Protection Law) policy in our selection processes to provide security and transparency regarding candidates applying for positions to join our team.

If you have any questions or want to learn more, please read our privacy policies: https://monks.com/

